//     the truth: (0,0) is the handle COINCIDENT with the anchor, i.e. "no handle,
//     the segment is a straight line". With absolute handles an anchor decoded
//     without in_/out_ would have its handles at the node's ORIGIN, i.e. a curve
//     that crashes into it: the most common case of all (a corner point) would be
//     the only one not representable at zero, and every writer would have to
//     remember to fill all six fields even when they are not needed.
//     It is also the reason most formats keep them relative.
//     The price -- an addition in the renderer -- is paid in a single place
